Restore the lap-record rectangle height's original image WORD.

View_BestLaps @0x44ffc0 loads DWORD [0x469568] then SAR 16 at
0x4500bc..0x4500c4: this is the signed height WORD at 0x46956a.
Its original descriptor is (-120,-38,232,95). The decompiler's sRam0046956a
had only a host global declaration/definition and no GIMG alias, so the steady
menu passed zero height to Draw_Semi_Trans_Poly. Rotation already reads the
same packed descriptor correctly; the table background vanished after entry.

Map that missing symbol to the actual short in the original game image.
The lap-record menu comparison checks all seven road tracks and reopening
through real keys, using a configuration produced and loaded by the original.

--- a/dd2_symbols.h
+++ b/dd2_symbols.h
@@ -257,1 +257,1 @@
-extern int sRam0046956a;
+#define sRam0046956a (*(short*)GIMG(0x0046956a))
